    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "I don't think this is it. I've tried running this file and it does return code 1.\r\nthe issue comes from [here](https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/blob/4ff0392767bfc7a2398b649b2f9362ddb9a8cc75/scripts/release/build-experimental-typescript.js#L23), where the code 1 returned by shell.exec is ignored.\r\n\r\nPer [exec](https://www.npmjs.com/package/shelljs#examples) docs, \r\n\r\n```js\r\n// Run external tool synchronously\r\nif (shell.exec('git commit -am \"Auto-commit\"').code !== 0) {\r\n  shell.echo('Error: Git commit failed');\r\n  shell.exit(1);\r\n}\r\n```\r\nthis would effectively make sure that `scripts/release/build-experimental-typescript.js` return code 1 if any of the exec inside do.",
    "commit_id": "ad9632d007224f9ea48bd706e0e9c94a05036467",
    "created_at": "2021-07-15T11:55:28Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -61,5 +61,6 @@ if (!result.succeeded) {\n       ` and ${result.warningCount} warnings`\n   );\n \n-  process.exitCode = 1;\n+  // eslint-disable-next-line no-process-exit\n+  process.exit(1);",
